 "profile_id": "naledi",
 "profile_name": "Naledi Local Municipality (Vryburg, North West)",
 "short_name": "Naledi",
 "_doc": "NALEDI LM (Vryburg, NW) - ledger/statement layout, account [number removed], dept code VRYM. Verified against 9 bills (2025/08 - 2026/07). All 9 have a real text layer; ocr='never' and ocr='auto' give byte-identical text, so nothing here is OCR-sourced. LAYOUT: the first text on the page is the ADDRESSEE block (TELKOM SA LTD / C/O TFMC PTY LTD / PRIVATE BAG X137 / CENTURION / 0046) - that is Telkom, NOT the issuer. The municipality's own identity is further down: the two masthead lines 'VRYBURG MUNICIPALITY' (remittance/bank block) and 'NALEDI MUNICIPALITY' (statement masthead, followed by dept code + account number). The bill prints the label 'VAT Reg. #:' with NOTHING after it - Naledi genuinely publishes no VAT registration number on this statement - so the fingerprint is the masthead string 'NALEDI MUNICIPALITY' (verified: present on 9/9 Naledi bills and on 0 of the other 210 bills in the Telkom tree). Never fingerprint on TELKOM SA LTD / PRIVATE BAG X137 / CENTURION / 4680101146 - those are on nearly every bill in the portfolio. TWO NUMBERS WORTH KNOWING: the line 'VRYBURG MUNICIPALITY  <n>  <amount>' carries the STATEMENT/INVOICE NUMBER and the WHOLE-ACCOUNT VAT TOTAL (verified to the cent on 9/9 as 15/115 of the VAT-bearing charges); the bare-date line under the masthead row is the DUE DATE. HEADER AGING ROW is '[30-day] [current charges incl VAT] ... [total due]' - the middle figure equals the sum of every ledger charge line incl VAT on 7/9 bills (2025/08 is reduced by a 'Transfers:' line, 2026/04 prints only '.00'). METER TABLE ('Tp. Meter No. Previous New Reading Factor Consumption Period Daily Aver'): Tp W = water, E = kWh registers (suffix OP/S/P = off-peak/standard/peak), K = the kVA demand register. Readings never carry a decimal point; the Consumption column always does ('.000') - that is what separates them when the Previous column is blank (blank Previous happens on 5 of 9 bills). Period prints DD/MM-DD/MM only, no year, and is kept exactly as printed. LEDGER TABLE ('Service type Tariff Consumption Basic'): every charge row prints amount EX VAT with FIVE decimals, then amount INCL VAT with TWO decimals, then the VAT which is RIGHT-TRUNCATED by the column width (129.0, 42.3, 8235.7) and must never be read as a value. Two independently printed columns therefore exist per row, which is the genuine identity check: sum(ex VAT) x 1.15 == sum(incl VAT). Services interleave in ARBITRARY order in that one table (SEWER / REFUSE / WATER / ELECTRICITY / ELEC.TOU / PSI), so electricity is the only positional section and water, sewerage, refuse and rates are OVERLAY sections over the same span - separation is enforced by line-anchored patterns, not by position. On one bill (2025/08) the ledger table is SPLIT BY THE PAGE BREAK with the whole page-2 header block in between and the STANDARD/PEAK rows after it; the electricity section therefore runs to end of document. SEWER prints only the incl-VAT and VAT columns (no ex-VAT figure), so sewer ex VAT is computed as incl - VAT. PSI ('[number removed] @ .00229' = property valuation @ cent-in-rand / 12) is ASSESSMENT RATES and is VAT-exempt - it is deliberately kept out of every electricity column. NOT PRINTED ANYWHERE: reading type (Actual/Estimate), notified max demand, cash/security-held. 'Deposit:' and 'Guarantee:' labels are printed but always blank on these 9 bills. The number 155 printed on the 'Erf:' line is constant on all 9 bills while billed kVA varies 116-155; it is captured as the erf/stand descriptor and is NOT claimed as an NMD - if Edwin can confirm it is the notified maximum demand, map nmd_kva to naledi_erf_2. RULE ZERO: no electricity-only ex-VAT total is printed on this bill, so total_ex_vat_r is the sum of the five electricity charge rows and the reconcile check is CIRCULAR - it proves nothing. The real checks are (a) sum(ex VAT) x 1.15 == sum(incl VAT) per row and in total, (b) the printed account VAT on the VRYBURG MUNICIPALITY line == 15/115 of (aging 'current' figure - PSI), (c) each ledger kWh bucket == the matching meter register's printed Consumption.",
